# @map map.cite: how to cite the repository and its measurements: GitHub's "Cite this repository" reads this file
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this tool or its measurements, please cite it as below."
title: "grepless: a code map and a pre-tool hook for AI coding agents"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: mars1571
repository-code: "https://github.com/mars1571/grepless"
url: "https://mars1571.github.io/grepless/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A code map for AI coding agents: a one-line tag above each block of code says what the block is for, a tool
  builds a map from the tags and the code, the agent asks the map a round of questions per call, and a pre-tool
  hook refuses grep, cat and sed on the code. Implementations in Python, Node, Go and Rust; hooks for Claude Code,
  OpenAI Codex, Cursor, GitHub Copilot and Gemini CLI. Includes measurements of 113 Claude Code sessions.
keywords:
  - AI coding agents
  - code map
  - context window
  - prompt caching
  - token usage
  - Claude Code
  - OpenAI Codex
  - Cursor
  - GitHub Copilot
  - Gemini CLI
  - AGENTS.md
